>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Split`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.Split : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as a local split rule for one extension simplifier call.
`Split th` adds `th` as `simpExtLib.add_split` does. Malformed rules are
ignored with a warning. No persistent attribute is claimed and no theorem-set
data is exported. Use the ML constructor or qualified `simpMarker$Split`
constant; no unqualified parser mapping is installed.

Nested requirement and bounded wrappers are processed before the directive.
A bound qualifies the directive; it does not install the marker as a rewrite
or count split applications. Generic marker tactics do not interpret this
simplifier-owned extension.

### Failure

Construction never fails. Enclosing requirement checks can fail when processed.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ext_bool_ss
     [BoundedRewrites.Once (simpExtLib.Req0
       (simpExtLib.Split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)))]
     ([], “P (case x of NONE => 0 | SOME n => n + 1) : bool”) c;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.add_split`](#simpExtLib.add_split),
[`splitLib.SPLIT_TAC`](#splitLib.SPLIT_TAC),
[`simpExtLib.ExclX`](#simpExtLib.ExclX).
